IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sca-nouns`
IMPORT `sca-p1-preliminary`

-- State Courts Act 1970 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition -- LAYER 1, PART 3: APPOINTMENTS, POWERS AND DUTIES (ss 8A to 18).
-- The sentences that only appoint (ss 8A(1), 9(1), 10(1), 11(1), 12(1), 14, 18) are machinery (boards, offices and their staffing) and have no rule here;
-- the qualifications, the status that follows from an appointment, the powers and duties of the officers, and the oaths are encoded.
-- A year count is the complete years the person has been "a qualified person as defined in section 2 of the Legal Profession Act 1966" (a borrowed term, asked as a number).

§ `Section 8A -- the Presiding Judge of the State Courts`

-- src:581 | (2) Despite any other written law, the Presiding Judge of the State
-- src:582 | Courts may sit in any State Court and act as a judge (however
-- src:583 | described) thereof, in which case the Presiding Judge has all the
-- src:584 | jurisdiction, power and privileges of such a judge.
@ref s 8A(2) (src:581-584)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an office or post`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(2) the holder may sit in any State Court and act as a judge of it with all the jurisdiction, power and privileges of such a judge` MEANS
    CONSIDER holder
    WHEN `Presiding Judge of the State Courts` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "the Presiding Judge of the State Courts" and says nothing of any other holder
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:591 | (3) A Supreme Court Judge or a Judicial Commissioner may,
-- src:592 | during the period of his or her appointment as the Presiding Judge of
-- src:593 | the State Courts, continue to sit in the General Division of the High
-- src:594 | Court, the Appellate Division of the High Court or the Court of
-- src:595 | Appeal in accordance with the Constitution.
@ref s 8A(3) (src:591-595)
GIVEN `the person is a Supreme Court Judge or a Judicial Commissioner appointed as the Presiding Judge of the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is during the period of the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(3) the person may continue to sit in the General Division of the High Court, the Appellate Division of the High Court or the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "A Supreme Court Judge or a Judicial Commissioner" appointed as the Presiding Judge
        IF NOT (`the person is a Supreme Court Judge or a Judicial Commissioner appointed as the Presiding Judge of the State Courts`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `it is during the period of the appointment` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, during the period of his or her appointment as the Presiding Judge ... continue to sit" (a period fixed in its own words: outside it the answer is JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:599 | (4) Any person appointed to be the Presiding Judge of the State
-- src:600 | Courts is, although the period of his or her appointment as such has
-- src:601 | expired or his or her appointment as such has been revoked, in
-- src:602 | relation to any case heard by him or her as a judge (however
-- src:603 | described) of a State Court, to continue to sit as such a judge for the
-- src:604 | purpose of giving judgment or otherwise.
@ref s 8A(4) (src:599-604)
GIVEN `the person was appointed to be the Presiding Judge of the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment has expired or has been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case was heard by the person as a judge of a State Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(4) the person continues to sit as a judge of the State Court to give judgment or otherwise in the case` MEANS
    IF `the person was appointed to be the Presiding Judge of the State Courts` AND `the appointment has expired or has been revoked` AND `the case was heard by the person as a judge of a State Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about a person appointed Presiding Judge whose appointment has expired or been revoked, "in relation to any case heard by him or her"
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 9 to 12 -- qualifications and status of District Judges, Magistrates and the registrar`

-- src:618 | (3) A person must not be appointed to be or to act as a District Judge
-- src:619 | unless he or she has been for not less than 7 years a qualified person as
-- src:620 | defined in section 2 of the Legal Profession Act 1966.
@ref s 9(3) (src:618-620)
GIVEN `complete years as a qualified person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(3) the person may be appointed to be or to act as a District Judge` MEANS
    IF `complete years as a qualified person` AT LEAST 7
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person must not be appointed ... unless he or she has been for not less than 7 years a qualified person" bars the person with fewer years; seven years lifts the bar but grants no appointment (QA: a lifted bar grants nothing), and s 9(1) is the power to appoint
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person must not be appointed to be or to act as a District Judge unless he or she has been for not less than 7 years a qualified person"
         JUST FALSE

-- src:624 | (3A) Despite subsection (3), a person may be appointed to be or to
-- src:625 | act as a District Judge if —
-- src:627 | (a) the person has been for not less than 5 years a qualified
-- src:628 | person as defined in section 2 of the Legal Profession
-- src:629 | Act 1966; and
-- src:631 | (b) the Chief Justice, after having regard to the qualifications
-- src:632 | and experience of the person, is of the opinion that the
-- src:633 | person is suitable to be appointed as a District Judge.
@ref s 9(3A)(a) and (b) (src:624-633)
GIVEN `complete years as a qualified person` IS A NUMBER
      `the Chief Justice, having regard to the qualifications and experience of the person, is of the opinion that the person is suitable to be appointed as a District Judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(3A) the person may be appointed to be or to act as a District Judge despite subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `complete years as a qualified person` AT LEAST 5 AND `the Chief Justice, having regard to the qualifications and experience of the person, is of the opinion that the person is suitable to be appointed as a District Judge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person may be appointed ... if — (a) ... not less than 5 years ...; and (b) the Chief Justice ... is of the opinion that the person is suitable" (a failed "if" is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
         JUST FALSE

-- src:637 | (4) Any person appointed to be or to act as a District Judge is,
-- src:638 | although the period of his or her appointment has expired or his or her
-- src:639 | appointment has been revoked, to sit as a District Judge for the
-- src:644 | purpose of giving judgment or otherwise in relation to any case heard
-- src:645 | by him or her.
@ref s 9(4) (src:637-645)
GIVEN `the person was appointed to be or to act as a District Judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment has expired or has been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case was heard by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(4) the person is to sit as a District Judge for the purpose of giving judgment or otherwise in the case` MEANS
    IF `the person was appointed to be or to act as a District Judge` AND `the appointment has expired or has been revoked` AND `the case was heard by the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about a person appointed to be or to act as a District Judge whose appointment has expired or been revoked, "in relation to any case heard by him or her"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:647 | (5) Every person appointed to be or to act as a District Judge is ex
-- src:648 | officio a Magistrate.
@ref s 9(5) (src:647-648)
GIVEN `the person was appointed to be or to act as a District Judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(5) the person is ex officio a Magistrate` MEANS
    IF `the person was appointed to be or to act as a District Judge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person appointed to be or to act as a District Judge is ex officio a Magistrate" says nothing of anyone else
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:657 | (2) A person must not be appointed to be or to act as a Magistrate
-- src:658 | unless he or she has been for not less than 3 years a qualified person as
-- src:659 | defined in section 2 of the Legal Profession Act 1966.
@ref s 10(2) (src:657-659)
GIVEN `complete years as a qualified person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(2) the person may be appointed to be or to act as a Magistrate` MEANS
    IF `complete years as a qualified person` AT LEAST 3
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person must not be appointed ... unless he or she has been for not less than 3 years a qualified person"; three years lifts the bar but grants no appointment (QA), and s 10(1) is the power to appoint
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person must not be appointed to be or to act as a Magistrate unless he or she has been for not less than 3 years a qualified person"
         JUST FALSE

-- src:663 | (3) Despite subsection (2), a person may be appointed to be or to act
-- src:664 | as a Magistrate if —
-- src:666 | (a) the person has been for not less than one year a qualified
-- src:667 | person as defined in section 2 of the Legal Profession
-- src:668 | Act 1966; and
-- src:670 | (b) the Chief Justice, after having regard to the qualifications
-- src:671 | and experience of the person, is of the opinion that the
-- src:672 | person is suitable to be appointed as a Magistrate.
@ref s 10(3)(a) and (b) (src:663-672)
GIVEN `complete years as a qualified person` IS A NUMBER
      `the Chief Justice, having regard to the qualifications and experience of the person, is of the opinion that the person is suitable to be appointed as a Magistrate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(3) the person may be appointed to be or to act as a Magistrate despite subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `complete years as a qualified person` AT LEAST 1 AND `the Chief Justice, having regard to the qualifications and experience of the person, is of the opinion that the person is suitable to be appointed as a Magistrate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person may be appointed ... if — (a) ... not less than one year ...; and (b) the Chief Justice ... is of the opinion that the person is suitable" (a failed "if" is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
         JUST FALSE

-- src:681 | (2) Justices of the Peace have and may exercise such powers and
-- src:682 | perform such duties of a Magistrate as may be conferred on them by
-- src:683 | any written law.
@ref s 11(2) (src:681-683)
GIVEN `the power or duty is one of a Magistrate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written law has conferred it on Justices of the Peace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(2) Justices of the Peace have and may exercise the power or perform the duty of a Magistrate` MEANS
    IF `the power or duty is one of a Magistrate` AND `a written law has conferred it on Justices of the Peace`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Justices of the Peace have "such powers and perform such duties of a Magistrate as may be conferred on them by any written law"; one no written law has conferred is outside that grant
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:697 | (2) A person must not be appointed to be or to act as registrar unless
-- src:698 | he or she is a qualified person as defined in section 2 of the Legal
-- src:699 | Profession Act 1966, except that the Chief Justice may, in his or her
-- src:700 | discretion, appoint any person who is not a qualified person under
-- src:701 | that Act.
@ref s 12(2) (src:697-701)
GIVEN `the person is a qualified person as defined in section 2 of the Legal Profession Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Justice, in his or her discretion, appoints the person although the person is not a qualified person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2) the person may be appointed to be or to act as registrar` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person must not be appointed ... unless he or she is a qualified person" bars the unqualified; being qualified lifts the bar but grants no appointment (QA), and s 12(1) is the power to appoint
        IF `the person is a qualified person as defined in section 2 of the Legal Profession Act 1966` THEN NOTHING
        -- the "except that the Chief Justice may, in his or her discretion, appoint any person who is not a qualified person" is itself a grant of the power, so JUST TRUE (QA: the default would be NOTHING; this exception is a permission in its own words)
        IF `the Chief Justice, in his or her discretion, appoints the person although the person is not a qualified person` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person must not be appointed to be or to act as registrar unless he or she is a qualified person"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:703 | (3) The registrar and the deputy registrars are ex officio
-- src:704 | commissioners for oaths.
@ref s 12(3) (src:703-704)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an office or post`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(3) the holder is ex officio a commissioner for oaths` MEANS
    CONSIDER holder
    WHEN `Registrar of the State Courts` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Deputy registrar of the State Courts` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The registrar and the deputy registrars are ex officio commissioners for oaths" says nothing of any other holder
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:708 | 13. Subject to Rules of Court, all the powers and duties conferred
-- src:709 | and imposed on the registrar may be exercised by a deputy registrar.
@ref s 13 (src:708-709)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an office or post`
      `Rules of Court provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 the holder may exercise the powers and duties conferred and imposed on the registrar` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to Rules of Court" leaves the position to Rules of Court that are not among the sources
        IF `Rules of Court provide otherwise` THEN NOTHING
        IF holder EQUALS `Deputy registrar of the State Courts` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about a deputy registrar and says nothing of any other holder
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Sections 15 and 15A -- bailiffs and process servers`

-- src:723 | 15.—(1) The bailiffs and process servers are to —
-- src:725 | (a) execute all writs, summonses, warrants, orders, notices and
-- src:726 | other mandatory processes of the State Courts given to
-- src:727 | them;
-- src:729 | (b) make a return of the same together with the manner of the
-- src:730 | execution thereof to the court from which the process
-- src:731 | issued; and
-- src:733 | (c) arrest and receive all such persons and property as are
-- src:734 | committed to the custody of the State Courts.
@ref s 15(1)(a) to (c) (src:723-734)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an office or post`
      duty IS A `Duty of a bailiff or process server`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(1) the holder is to do the duty` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "The bailiffs and process servers" and says nothing of any other holder
        IF NOT (holder EQUALS Bailiff OR holder EQUALS `Process server`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection lists three duties and does not say that bailiffs and process servers have no other duty
        IF duty EQUALS `Some other duty` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 15(1)(a) (src:723-734)
-- The duties of s 15(1) as regulative rules (no time limit and no consequence is stated, so none is written).
`s 15(1)(a) duty: bailiffs and process servers are to execute the processes given to them` MEANS
    PARTY `A bailiff or process server`
    MUST `execute a writ, summons, warrant, order, notice or other mandatory process`

@ref s 15(1)(b) (src:723-734)
`s 15(1)(b) duty: bailiffs and process servers are to make a return of the execution` MEANS
    PARTY `A bailiff or process server`
    MUST `make a return of the process and the manner of its execution to the court from which it issued`

@ref s 15(1)(c) (src:723-734)
`s 15(1)(c) duty: bailiffs and process servers are to arrest and receive the persons and property committed to custody` MEANS
    PARTY `A bailiff or process server`
    MUST `arrest and receive the persons and property committed to the custody of the State Courts`

-- src:740 | (2) The registrar may engage any auxiliary police officer appointed
-- src:741 | under the Police Force Act 2004*, any security agency, a provider of
-- src:742 | transport and of warehousing, a valuer, an estate agent, a broker, a
-- src:747 | solicitor or any other appropriate person to assist the bailiffs in the
-- src:748 | discharge of the bailiffs’ duties.
@ref s 15(2) (src:740-748)
GIVEN `the person is an auxiliary police officer, a security agency, a provider of transport and of warehousing, a valuer, an estate agent, a broker, a solicitor or another appropriate person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the engagement is to assist the bailiffs in the discharge of the bailiffs' duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(2) the registrar may engage the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is an auxiliary police officer, a security agency, a provider of transport and of warehousing, a valuer, an estate agent, a broker, a solicitor or another appropriate person` AND `the engagement is to assist the bailiffs in the discharge of the bailiffs' duties`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the registrar may engage the listed kinds "or any other appropriate person" to "assist the bailiffs"; whether a person is appropriate is for the registrar, and the subsection says nothing of an engagement for another purpose
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:756 | 15A.—(1) Subject to any directions that may be given by the
-- src:757 | Presiding Judge of the State Courts, the registrar may authorise a
-- src:758 | solicitor or a person employed by a solicitor to exercise the powers
-- src:759 | and perform the duties of a bailiff during such period or on such
-- src:760 | occasion as the registrar thinks fit and subject to such terms and
-- src:761 | conditions as the registrar may determine.
@ref s 15A(1) (src:756-761)
GIVEN `the person is a solicitor or a person employed by a solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Presiding Judge of the State Courts has given a direction that bars it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15A(1) the registrar may authorise the person to exercise the powers and perform the duties of a bailiff` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to any directions that may be given by the Presiding Judge of the State Courts"; a direction is not among the sources
        IF `the Presiding Judge of the State Courts has given a direction that bars it` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the person is a solicitor or a person employed by a solicitor` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the registrar may authorise "a solicitor or a person employed by a solicitor" and the subsection says nothing of anyone else
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:765 | (2) Section 68(2) applies to a solicitor or person authorised under
-- src:766 | subsection (1) as it applies to an officer of a State Court.
@ref s 15A(2) (src:765-766)
GIVEN `the person was authorised under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15A(2) section 68(2) applies to the person as it applies to an officer of a State Court` MEANS
    IF `the person was authorised under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "a solicitor or person authorised under subsection (1)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:772 | 16. The bailiffs in executing any enforcement order for seizure and
-- src:773 | sale of property, any other enforcement order or any writ of distress
-- src:774 | may effect an entry into any building, and for that purpose, if
-- src:775 | necessary, may break open any outer or inner door or window of the
-- src:776 | building or any receptacle therein, using such force as is reasonably
-- src:777 | necessary to effect an entry.
@ref s 16 (src:772-777)
GIVEN `the holder is a bailiff` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the bailiff is executing an enforcement order for seizure and sale of property, any other enforcement order or a writ of distress` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16 the bailiff may effect an entry into a building` MEANS
    IF `the holder is a bailiff` AND `the bailiff is executing an enforcement order for seizure and sale of property, any other enforcement order or a writ of distress`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given to "The bailiffs in executing any enforcement order ... or any writ of distress"; it says nothing of another person or another occasion
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 16 (src:772-777)
GIVEN `it is necessary to effect an entry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the force used is no more than is reasonably necessary to effect an entry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16 the bailiff may break open an outer or inner door or window of the building or any receptacle in it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if necessary, may break open" (a failed "if" is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a)); the Act gives no power to break open what need not be broken to enter
        IF NOT (`it is necessary to effect an entry`) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the force used is no more than is reasonably necessary to effect an entry` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "using such force as is reasonably necessary to effect an entry"; force beyond that is outside the grant, which does not say that it is forbidden
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Section 17 -- oaths`

-- src:783 | 17.—(1) All judicial officers and any other officers of the State
-- src:784 | Courts as may be required by the Chief Justice, before exercising the
-- src:785 | functions of their respective offices, are to take and subscribe the
-- src:786 | appropriate oath of office and allegiance set out in the Schedule.
@ref s 17(1) (src:783-786)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an office or post`
      `the Chief Justice has required the officer to take the oath` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) the officer is to take and subscribe the oath before exercising the functions of the office` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 "judicial officer" the holder is a judicial officer` holder EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the Chief Justice has required the officer to take the oath` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "All judicial officers and any other officers of the State Courts as may be required by the Chief Justice"; an officer who is neither is outside it
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 17(1) (src:783-786)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an office or post`
      `took the oath before exercising the functions of the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) the oath was taken and subscribed before the functions of the office were exercised as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `took the oath before exercising the functions of the office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "are to take and subscribe" is a bare requirement (QB) and section 17 does not say what follows when the oath was not taken first
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 17(1) (src:783-786)
`s 17(1) duty: a judicial officer is to take and subscribe the oath before exercising the functions` MEANS
    PARTY `A judicial officer`
    MUST `take and subscribe the oath of office`

-- src:2443 | 1. OATHS OF OFFICE AND ALLEGIANCE OF A JUDICIAL OFFICER
-- src:2445 | I, , having been appointed to the office of
-- src:2447 | do solemnly swear (or affirm) that I will faithfully discharge my
-- src:2449 | judicial duties and I will do right to all manner of people after the laws and usages
-- src:2451 | of the Republic of Singapore without fear or favour, affection or ill will to the
-- src:2453 | best of my ability, and I will be faithful and bear true allegiance to the Republic
-- src:2455 | of Singapore.
-- src:2457 | Taken and subscribed before me at this day of .
-- src:2459 | Officer Administering the Oath
@ref Schedule para 1 (src:2443-2459)
`Schedule para 1 the oath of office and allegiance of a judicial officer` MEANS
    `Oath form`
        WITH `item of the Schedule` IS 1
             `taken by` IS "a judicial officer"
             words IS "1. OATHS OF OFFICE AND ALLEGIANCE OF A JUDICIAL OFFICER I, , having been appointed to the office of do solemnly swear (or affirm) that I will faithfully discharge my judicial duties and I will do right to all manner of people after the laws and usages of the Republic of Singapore without fear or favour, affection or ill will to the best of my ability, and I will be faithful and bear true allegiance to the Republic of Singapore. Taken and subscribed before me at this day of . Officer Administering the Oath"

-- src:2461 | 2. OATH OF OFFICE OF AN INTERPRETER
-- src:2463 | I, , having been appointed an interpreter of the
-- src:2465 | Court do solemnly swear (or affirm) that I will faithfully interpret,
-- src:2467 | translate and transcribe from the language into the English
-- src:2469 | language and from the English language into the language to the
-- src:2471 | best of my knowledge, skill and ability and without fear or favour, affection or ill
-- src:2473 | will.
-- src:2480 | Taken and subscribed before me at this
-- src:2484 | Officer Administering the Oath
@ref Schedule para 2 (src:2461-2484)
`Schedule para 2 the oath of office of an interpreter` MEANS
    `Oath form`
        WITH `item of the Schedule` IS 2
             `taken by` IS "an interpreter"
             words IS "2. OATH OF OFFICE OF AN INTERPRETER I, , having been appointed an interpreter of the Court do solemnly swear (or affirm) that I will faithfully interpret, translate and transcribe from the language into the English language and from the English language into the language to the best of my knowledge, skill and ability and without fear or favour, affection or ill will. Taken and subscribed before me at this . Officer Administering the Oath"

-- src:2486 | 3. OATH OF OFFICE OF OTHER OFFICER OF A COURT
-- src:2488 | I, , having been appointed to the office of
-- src:2490 | in the Court do solemnly swear (or affirm) that I
-- src:2492 | will not use or exercise my office corruptly during the time that I remain therein,
-- src:2494 | neither will I take or accept by any means whatsoever any fee or reward from any
-- src:2496 | person or persons, but will truly and faithfully and with convenient speed execute
-- src:2498 | the duties assigned to me and will make true and faithful returns as to the manner
-- src:2500 | and time of the execution of all writs, summonses, warrants, orders, notices and
-- src:2502 | other mandatory processes given to me.
-- src:2504 | Taken and subscribed before me at this day of
-- src:2507 | Officer Administering the Oath
@ref Schedule para 3 (src:2486-2507)
`Schedule para 3 the oath of office of other officer of a court` MEANS
    `Oath form`
        WITH `item of the Schedule` IS 3
             `taken by` IS "an officer of a court other than a judicial officer or an interpreter"
             words IS "3. OATH OF OFFICE OF OTHER OFFICER OF A COURT I, , having been appointed to the office of in the Court do solemnly swear (or affirm) that I will not use or exercise my office corruptly during the time that I remain therein, neither will I take or accept by any means whatsoever any fee or reward from any person or persons, but will truly and faithfully and with convenient speed execute the duties assigned to me and will make true and faithful returns as to the manner and time of the execution of all writs, summonses, warrants, orders, notices and other mandatory processes given to me. Taken and subscribed before me at this day of . Officer Administering the Oath"

@ref Schedule (the appropriate oath under section 17(1)) (src:2443-2507)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an office or post`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Oath form`
`Schedule the oath that section 17(1) requires of the holder` MEANS
    CONSIDER holder
    WHEN `District Judge` THEN JUST `Schedule para 1 the oath of office and allegiance of a judicial officer`
    WHEN Magistrate THEN JUST `Schedule para 1 the oath of office and allegiance of a judicial officer`
    WHEN `Registrar of the State Courts` THEN JUST `Schedule para 1 the oath of office and allegiance of a judicial officer`
    WHEN `Deputy registrar of the State Courts` THEN JUST `Schedule para 1 the oath of office and allegiance of a judicial officer`
    WHEN Interpreter THEN JUST `Schedule para 2 the oath of office of an interpreter`
    WHEN Bailiff THEN JUST `Schedule para 3 the oath of office of other officer of a court`
    WHEN `Process server` THEN JUST `Schedule para 3 the oath of office of other officer of a court`
    WHEN `Commissioner for oaths` THEN JUST `Schedule para 3 the oath of office of other officer of a court`
    WHEN `Another officer of a State Court` THEN JUST `Schedule para 3 the oath of office of other officer of a court`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Schedule sets out three oaths and does not say which of them a Presiding Judge, a Justice of the Peace or a Supreme Court Judge takes
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:790 | (2) The oath mentioned in subsection (1) may be taken and
-- src:791 | subscribed before the Presiding Judge of the State Courts, the
-- src:792 | Presiding Judge of the Family Justice Courts, a Supreme Court Judge
-- src:793 | or a Judicial Commissioner.
@ref s 17(2) (src:790-793)
GIVEN before IS A `Person administering an oath`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(2) the oath may be taken and subscribed before the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER before
    WHEN `Someone else` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection says the oath "may be taken and subscribed before" four named office holders and does not say "only"
        NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:800 | (2A) To avoid doubt, where an oath is required to be taken and
-- src:801 | subscribed under subsection (1), a person may take and subscribe the
-- src:802 | oath by appearing before the Presiding Judge of the State Courts, the
-- src:803 | Presiding Judge of the Family Justice Courts, a Supreme Court Judge
-- src:804 | or a Judicial Commissioner through a live video link or live television
-- src:805 | link created using a remote communication technology that allows
-- src:806 | the Presiding Judge of the State Courts, Presiding Judge of the Family
-- src:807 | Justice Courts, Supreme Court Judge or Judicial Commissioner (as
-- src:808 | the case may be) to —
-- src:810 | (a) maintain visual contact and communicate with the person
-- src:811 | taking the oath, and any interpreter present, throughout the
-- src:812 | process;
-- src:814 | (b) confirm the identity of the person taking the oath and any
-- src:815 | interpreter present; and
-- src:817 | (c) verify by inspection the oath to be subscribed.
@ref s 17(2A)(a) to (c) (src:800-817)
GIVEN `the person appears before the administering judge through a live video link or live television link` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technology allows the judge to maintain visual contact and communicate with the person and any interpreter throughout the process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technology allows the judge to confirm the identity of the person and any interpreter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technology allows the judge to verify by inspection the oath to be subscribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(2A) the person may take and subscribe the oath by appearing through a live video link or live television link` MEANS
    IF `the person appears before the administering judge through a live video link or live television link`
       AND `the technology allows the judge to maintain visual contact and communicate with the person and any interpreter throughout the process`
       AND `the technology allows the judge to confirm the identity of the person and any interpreter`
       AND `the technology allows the judge to verify by inspection the oath to be subscribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the oath may be taken through a link "created using a remote communication technology that allows" the three things; a link without them is outside this "to avoid doubt" provision, which does not say the oath may not be taken that way
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:821 | (3) Where the oath is taken before the Presiding Judge of the State
-- src:822 | Courts, he or she is to —
-- src:824 | (a) enter in the record of the State Courts that the oath was
-- src:825 | duly administered and taken before him or her; and
-- src:827 | (b) transmit a certified copy of the entry to the Registrar of the
-- src:828 | Supreme Court.
@ref s 17(3)(a) and (b) (src:821-828)
GIVEN `the oath was taken before the Presiding Judge of the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Presiding Judge entered in the record of the State Courts that the oath was duly administered and taken before him or her` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Presiding Judge transmitted a certified copy of the entry to the Registrar of the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(3) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts has entered the oath in the record and transmitted a certified copy as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the oath was taken before the Presiding Judge of the State Courts` AND `the Presiding Judge entered in the record of the State Courts that the oath was duly administered and taken before him or her` AND `the Presiding Judge transmitted a certified copy of the entry to the Registrar of the Supreme Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "he or she is to" is a bare requirement (QB), and the subsection is about an oath taken before the Presiding Judge of the State Courts; it does not say what follows when either step is not done
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:832 | (4) Where the oath is taken before the Presiding Judge of the Family
-- src:833 | Justice Courts, he or she is to —
-- src:835 | (a) enter in the record of the Family Justice Courts that the
-- src:836 | oath was duly administered and taken before him or her;
-- src:838 | (b) transmit a certified copy of the entry to the Registrar of the
-- src:839 | Supreme Court; and
-- src:841 | (c) transmit a certified copy of the entry to the Presiding Judge
-- src:842 | of the State Courts.
@ref s 17(4)(a) to (c) (src:832-842)
GIVEN `the oath was taken before the Presiding Judge of the Family Justice Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Presiding Judge entered in the record of the Family Justice Courts that the oath was duly administered and taken before him or her` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Presiding Judge transmitted a certified copy of the entry to the Registrar of the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Presiding Judge transmitted a certified copy of the entry to the Presiding Judge of the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(4) the Presiding Judge of the Family Justice Courts has entered the oath in the record and transmitted the certified copies as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the oath was taken before the Presiding Judge of the Family Justice Courts` AND `the Presiding Judge entered in the record of the Family Justice Courts that the oath was duly administered and taken before him or her` AND `the Presiding Judge transmitted a certified copy of the entry to the Registrar of the Supreme Court` AND `the Presiding Judge transmitted a certified copy of the entry to the Presiding Judge of the State Courts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "he or she is to" is a bare requirement (QB), and the subsection is about an oath taken before the Presiding Judge of the Family Justice Courts; it does not say what follows when a step is not done
    ELSE NOTHING
